course: dictionary
lesson: 2911
title: Doze and dozing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To doze is to sleep lightly for a short time, often during the day. The word can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it has four forms: doze, dozes, dozed, dozing. As a noun, a doze is one short, light sleep. «One afternoon, while the Rat dozes in his armchair hunting for rhymes» tells you the Rat is asleep, but not deeply asleep.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Then she began to doze and dreamed she was walking hand in hand with Dinah.» Alice starts to doze, and then she dreams. So doze comes before a dream, which means she is drifting into sleep, not yet in deep sleep. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try "sleep lightly" in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Doze has friends. You can doze off, have a doze, or go dozing in the sun. «Kangaroos doze in the shade a few steps away» shows animals resting quietly, not running or playing. When you see doze in a story, think of a person or animal resting in a quiet, calm place.
fact: To doze means to sleep lightly for a short time.
fact: A doze is a short, light sleep.
fact: Doze is a verb: doze, dozes, dozed, dozing. A doze is also a noun.
fact: «Doze off» means to fall asleep lightly without meaning to.
fact: Sleeping well at night helps children stay awake and alert in class, so they do not doze off during lessons.
exercise: «One afternoon, while the Rat dozes in his armchair hunting for rhymes, the Mole quietly decides to go out.» What does dozes mean here? | *Sleeps lightly for a short time | Eats a big meal | Runs fast around the room | Reads a book aloud
exercise: «In the Australian walkabout, kangaroos doze in the shade a few steps away.» What are the kangaroos doing? | Jumping over the fence | Racing the keepers | Eating from a bowl | *Resting lightly in the shade
exercise: In «have a doze», is doze a noun or a verb? | Verb | Adjective | *Noun | Adverb
test: «Horses can doze standing up because locking joints in their legs hold them without effort.» What does doze mean? | Run very fast | Wake up with a shout | *Sleep lightly for a short time while standing | Lie down and sleep all night
test: Which phrase means falling asleep lightly without meaning to? | Wake up | Dash off | *Doze off | Race ahead
exam: «Sleepy, Alice kept asking questions, and then she began to doze and dreamed she was walking hand in hand with Dinah.» Which word tells us Alice is starting to sleep lightly? | Walking | Dreamed | Asking | *Doze
